-- title:
--   Hecke endomorphisms act additively on the geometric special fibre
-- statement:
--   Throughout, `SchemeHomOver g f` denotes the type of morphisms $\varphi$ with $\varphi$ followed by $f$ equal to $g$; a `RelativePic0Designation` over a ring $R$ for a curve $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ is a scheme $P$ together with a structure morphism `toBase` $: P \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and a section `zeroSection`; and `RepresentsRelSubPic c ε P D` is the datum of a rigidified line bundle `poincare` over `D.toBase` satisfying the cut $P$, the universal property that every rigidified line bundle over a base $t$ satisfying $P$ is the pullback of `poincare` along a unique element of `SchemeHomOver t D.toBase` (up to isomorphism of the underlying bundles), and an isomorphism between the pullback along the zero section and the unit bundle. The cut used is `algEquivZeroCut c ε`, whose condition on a rigidified bundle is the predicate `FibrewiseAlgEquivZero`.
--
--   Arithmetic data. Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ given by `hK` as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), equipped with an algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be non-zero with $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (`hj`). Write $\pi =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) for the resulting two-chart model over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper.
--
--   The geometric special fibre. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra, and let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral. Let $i_1, i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1$, $C_2$ over $k$ into the base change of $\pi$ to $k$, such that every point of the fibre product of $\pi$ with $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$ (`hcover`), the fibre product of $i_1$ with $i_2$ is reduced (`hred`), and $n$ is its number of points (`hn`), with $0 < n$ (`hn0`).
--
--   Sections and relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$. Let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $\pi$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ sections of $c_1, c_2$, with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base-changed section $\varepsilon_k$ (`hε₁`). Let $D$ be a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation for $\pi$ over $A$, representing the cut functor for $(\pi, \varepsilon)$ (`hrep`), with `D.toBase` smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`). The hypothesis `hreps` asserts that `D.baseChange k` represents the corresponding functor for the base-changed curve and section over $k$, and `hPk` that its Poincaré bundle is isomorphic to the base change `BaseChange.ofR` of the pullback of `hrep.some.poincare` along `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A k)`. Similarly $D_1$ and $D_2$ represent the functors for $(c_1, \varepsilon_1)$ and $(c_2, \varepsilon_2)$ (`hrep₁`, `hrep₂`). Let $\nu_2$ be a morphism from `(D.baseChange k).toBase` to `D₂.toBase` over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ such that, for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and every $a \in$ `SchemeHomOver t (D.baseChange k).toBase`, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hrep₂.some` along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification (along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` and the second projection) of the pullback along `curveChange i₂` of the pullback of `hreps.poincare` along $a$ (`hν₂`); thus $\nu_2$ induces on points the pullback of line bundles along $i_2$.
--
--   The generic fibre over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` carry compatible $A$- and $L$-algebra structures. Let $M_\eta$ be a `CurveModel` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) — a smooth proper integral curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with a ring isomorphism of that field onto its function field compatible with scalars, a bijection from its closed points onto the places, the stalk-range condition, and the property that finite sets of points lie in affine opens — and let $e_\eta$ be an isomorphism from $M_\eta.C$ to the base change of $\pi$ along $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`). The preimage under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) is assumed non-empty, and `hMηpin` asserts that for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) the germ of $a$ at the generic point, transported by `Mη.ffEquiv.symm`, has as Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise image under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $a$ viewed in $K \subseteq L((q))$. The hypothesis `hgal` asserts Galois equivariance of the place dictionary: for every $\mathbb{Q}$-automorphism $g$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, then `Mη.pointEquivPlace x'` is the translate of `Mη.pointEquivPlace x` by [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54).
--
--   The combinatorial special fibre. Let $G$ be a [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9): abelian groups $J^0_s$, $J_I$, $J_E$, a subgroup `torus` of $J^0_s$ and a surjective homomorphism `proj` $: J^0_s \to J_I \times J_E$ with kernel `torus`. Let `pts`, `ptsI`, `ptsE` be bijections of $J^0_s$, $J_I$, $J_E$ with the $k$-points of `(D.baseChange k).toBase`, `D₁.toBase`, `D₂.toBase` respectively. The hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE` state that each of these dictionaries is additive at the level of Poincaré pullbacks: the pullback along the image of a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks along the images of the summands. The hypothesis `hproj` states that for every $x \in J^0_s$ the first component of `proj x` corresponds under `ptsI` to `pts x` followed by `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom i₁.1 i₁.2 hε₁ hreps hrep₁.some`, and the second component corresponds under `ptsE` to `pts x` followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   The generic points dictionary and the Hecke endomorphisms. Let `gpts` be a bijection of [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group of degree-zero divisor classes of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) modulo principal divisors, with the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of `D.toBase` over $A$, carrying addition to the relative group law of `hrep.some` for the group cut `algEquivZeroGroupCut` (`hgadd`). Let $\varphi$ assign to each element $t$ of [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) $=$ `MvPolynomial (Nat.Primes ⊕ ℕ) ℤ` an endomorphism $\varphi(t)$ of `D.toBase` over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, such that post-composition with $\varphi(t)$ commutes with the relative group law on $T$-points for every base $s : T \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ (`hφmul`), and such that, for the Hecke module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129), `gpts (t • x)` is `gpts x` followed by $\varphi(t)$ for all $t$ and all $x$ (`hφpts`).
--
--   Abel–Jacobi data. The hypothesis `hDL` asserts representability over $L$ by `D.baseChange L`, `hPL` the corresponding Poincaré comparison, and `ajL` is a morphism from the base change of $\pi$ to $L$ to `(D.baseChange L).toBase` over $L$ with `hajLε`: the base-changed section $\varepsilon_L$ followed by `ajL` is the zero section; `hajL` characterises `ajL` as an Abel–Jacobi map: for every field $K'$, every $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of the base-changed curve, the pullback of `hDL.poincare` along $x$ followed by `ajL` is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the point $t$ followed by $\varepsilon_L$. Further, `kL` is a morphism between the base changes of $\pi$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and to $L$ compatible with both projections (`hkL₁`, `hkL₂`), `ajbar` is the composite of $e_\eta$, `kL`, `ajL` and `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A L)` (`hajbar`), lying over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ (`hajbar_over`); $\bar\varepsilon$ is a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $M_\eta.C$ inducing $\varepsilon$ (`hεbar`) and sent by `ajbar` to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`). Finally `hpts_aj` asserts the compatibility of `gpts` with `ajbar`: for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ inducing $\varepsilon$, there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ equal to the difference of the one-point divisors at the places of $x$ and of $s$ whose class satisfies `(gpts (Pic0.mk Dv)).1 = x.1 ≫ ajbar`.
--
--   Reduction data. Let $\mathfrak{P}$ ( `Pl` ) be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ in its non-units (`hPl`), let $\rho : A \to \mathfrak{P}$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion is the structure map $A \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hρ`), let $O$ be a subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ contained in $\mathfrak{P}$ (`hO`) with $\rho_O : A \to O$ satisfying the same compatibility (`hρO`), and let $\pi_k : \mathfrak{P} \to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism (`hπk`) with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ the structure map $A \to k$ (`hAlgk`).
--
--   Conclusion. For every $t \in$ [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) there exists an additive endomorphism $U_s : J^0_s \to J^0_s$ such that:
--
--   (i) for every $y \in J^0_s$, the morphism `(pts (Us y)).1` followed by `pullback.fst D.toBase (specMap A k)` equals `(pts y).1` followed by that projection and then by $\varphi(t)$;
--
--   (ii) for all $z, z'$ in `SchemeHomOver (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ρO)) D.toBase`, that is $O$-points of `D.toBase` over $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$, and all $y, y' \in J^0_s$: if `(pts y).1` followed by the projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\pi_k \circ (O \hookrightarrow \mathfrak{P})$ followed by $z$, if $z'$ equals $z$ followed by $\varphi(t)$, and if `(pts y').1` followed by the projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the same reduction map followed by $z'$, then $y' = U_s y$;
--
--   (iii) the same statement with $O$ replaced by $\mathfrak{P}$: for all $z, z'$ in `SchemeHomOver (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom ρ)) D.toBase` and all $y, y' \in J^0_s$, if `(pts y).1` followed by the projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by $z$, if $z' = z$ followed by $\varphi(t)$, and if `(pts y').1` followed by the projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\pi_k)$ followed by $z'$, then $y' = U_s y$.
--
--   This is the Néron mapping-property step for $J_1(Mp)$ in residue characteristic $p$: the $A$-endomorphisms $\varphi(t)$ of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ scheme of the two-chart model act on the $k$-points of the geometric special fibre through additive endomorphisms $U_s$ of $J^0_s$, and these endomorphisms are computed by reducing $O$-points or $\mathfrak{P}$-points. It is used by the later results that identify the action of the Hecke and diamond generators on the toric, étale and cuspidal parts of the special fibre.
